---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Contact | Podomy"
	description="Contact Podomy engineering about commercial licensing, assurance reviews, and consulting."
	currentPath="/contact/"
>
	<h1 class="page-title">Contact</h1>
	<p class="page-lead">
		Talk directly to the engineers building the software.
	</p>

	<section class="content-section" style="margin-top: 0;">
		<p class="body-p">
			No sales queue. No account manager. No bot.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			<strong><a href="mailto:contact@podomy.com" class="body-link">contact@podomy.com</a></strong>. We reply within 24 hours, usually much faster.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2 class="section-title">What happens next</h2>
		<ol class="numbered-list">
			<li>
				<span><strong>We talk.</strong> Your machines, network, and workloads. For existing code, request an assurance review.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span><strong>You evaluate.</strong> Docs or a pilot on your hardware. Free under AGPL.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span><strong>We sign an <abbr title="Master Services Agreement">MSA</abbr> and <abbr title="Statement of Work">SOW</abbr>.</strong> The <abbr title="Master Services Agreement">MSA</abbr> sets the terms. The <abbr title="Statement of Work">SOW</abbr> defines the pilot on your hardware and the acceptance test. We quote your tier. No negotiation theater.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span><strong>We make it work.</strong> We install it on your hardware and get it working. You sign off on the acceptance test. You pay only after signoff. Then you run it.</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span><strong>After signoff.</strong> Your license covers core patches. You run your fleet. Extra help is by the hour. New work means a new <abbr title="Statement of Work">SOW</abbr>.</span>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<p class="body-p">
		Your communications and deployment details stay private. For pricing, see <a href="/pricing/" class="body-link">Pricing</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
